WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:16.030
Aunt Polly sent Nancy to deliver the bad news to Mr.

2
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:21.474
Pendleton. Normally Nancy would have been excited to see inside his mysterious mansion.

3
00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:27.538
But now she was too upset to even glance around the library, where she waited for Mr.

4
00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:30.420
Pendleton. "Well?"

5
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.241
he said upon entering the room.

6
00:00:32.261 --> 00:00:38.025
"Sir, the New York doctor says Pollyanna will never walk again!"

7
00:00:40.086 --> 00:00:42.208
Mr. Pendleton sank into the nearest chair.

8
00:00:42.228 --> 00:00:44.389
"Poor little girl."

9
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.012
He covered his eyes with his hand and moaned.

10
00:00:48.032 --> 00:00:51.895
"My little prism girl!

11
00:00:51.915 --> 00:00:54.757
She'll never dance in the sunshine again."

12
00:00:57.238 --> 00:01:02.554
Nancy could not believe that John Pendleton—a grumpy miser— was showing such emotion.

13
00:01:04.175 --> 00:01:04.755
He looked up.

14
00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:08.217
"I hope Pollyanna doesn't know this horrible news."

15
00:01:09.618 --> 00:01:11.199
"That's the worst part, sir.

16
00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:12.580
She does."

17
00:01:17.923 --> 00:01:18.763
Nancy sobbed.

18
00:01:18.783 --> 00:01:22.525
"And she can't think of anything to be glad about."

19
00:01:22.545 --> 00:01:26.608
"I know how much she loves to play her Glad Game."

20
00:01:28.428 --> 00:01:32.470
"I tried to cheer her up by reminding her what she told Mrs.

21
00:01:32.551 --> 00:01:38.554
Snow. But she said it's one thing to tell a lifelong invalid how to play the game.

22
00:01:39.615 --> 00:01:42.636
And quite another when you're the lifelong invalid."

23
00:01:44.878 --> 00:01:49.340
Mr. Pendleton offered Nancy his handkerchief, and she wiped her eyes before continuing.

24
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.261
"Thank you, sir.

25
00:01:51.742 --> 00:01:55.304
Pollyanna used to say the game was more interesting when it was hard.

26
00:01:56.408 --> 00:01:59.891
But now she keeps dwelling on the fact that she'll never walk again.

27
00:01:59.911 --> 00:02:05.316
I must leave, sir, because Miss Polly needs me at home."

28
00:02:07.378 --> 00:02:09.279
Nancy hopped up but turned at the door.

29
00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:14.123
"Pollyanna feels bad that she can't bring Jimmy Bean to visit you.

30
00:02:15.304 --> 00:02:17.806
She fears he didn't make a good impression the first time."

31
00:02:18.827 --> 00:02:19.548
She hesitated.

32
00:02:19.568 --> 00:02:23.852
"I'm sure she'd be glad to hear that you were going to visit him."

33
00:02:25.248 --> 00:02:26.609
Mr. Pendleton shook his head.

34
00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:29.771
"I'm sorry, but I have no plans to see him."

35
00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:35.776
The entire town soon knew that Pollyanna would never walk again.

36
00:02:37.096 --> 00:02:41.540
Many people recognized Pollyanna as the cheerful girl who always greeted them with a smile.

37
00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.022
And almost everyone was familiar with the Glad Game.

38
00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:53.068
Aunt Polly was surprised by the number of visitors—friends and strangers—who arrived at her door.

39
00:02:54.324 --> 00:02:59.448
Many people were in tears as they handed Aunt Polly flowers or other gifts for Pollyanna.

40
00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:07.013
When John Pendleton arrived one day, he had an important message for Pollyanna.

41
00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:10.115
"Please tell her that I've seen Jimmy Bean.

42
00:03:11.096 --> 00:03:13.238
She'll be glad to know that I'm thinking of adopting him."

43
00:03:14.639 --> 00:03:17.801
Aunt Polly was so shocked that she couldn't control her reaction.

44
00:03:19.822 --> 00:03:20.783
"Jimmy Bean?"

45
00:03:21.443 --> 00:03:22.084
she gasped.

46
00:03:23.284 --> 00:03:26.405
"You're going to adopt that that boy?"

47
00:03:26.425 --> 00:03:30.107
"Yes, and I think Pollyanna will understand why."

48
00:03:32.888 --> 00:03:33.388
After Mr.

49
00:03:33.428 --> 00:03:36.890
Pendleton left, Aunt Polly went upstairs and delivered his message.

50
00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.072
"Mr. Pendleton said you'd be glad about this news."

51
00:03:42.653 --> 00:03:44.633
Pollyanna broke into a wide grin.

52
00:03:44.653 --> 00:03:48.275
"Glad? Of course I'm glad!

53
00:03:49.315 --> 00:03:53.302
Oh, Aunt Polly, I've wanted to find a place for Jimmy to live.

54
00:03:54.523 --> 00:03:55.143
And Mr.

55
00:03:55.183 --> 00:03:57.885
Pendleton's house is such a lovely place.

56
00:03:59.146 --> 00:04:00.987
Besides, I'm glad for Mr.

57
00:04:01.027 --> 00:04:03.809
Pendleton because he'll have a child's presence."

58
00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.091
"A what?"

59
00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:12.755
"Mr. Pendleton thinks it takes a spouse's hand and heart or a child's presence to make a house

60
00:04:12.796 --> 00:04:13.236
a home.

61
00:04:14.477 --> 00:04:16.158
Dr. Chilton thinks that too."

62
00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:18.900
Aunt Polly looked startled.

63
00:04:20.268 --> 00:04:21.449
"Dr. Chilton!

64
00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:23.330
How do you know what he thinks?"

65
00:04:25.151 --> 00:04:26.232
"He told me himself.

66
00:04:27.493 --> 00:04:30.755
He says the rooms where he lives aren't really a home."

67
00:04:33.357 --> 00:04:37.079
While Aunt Polly stared silently out the window, Pollyanna went on.

68
00:04:37.099 --> 00:04:41.622
"So I asked him why he didn't get a spouse's hand and heart."

69
00:04:41.642 --> 00:04:47.286
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly turned abruptly and shook her finger at Pollyanna.

70
00:04:47.306 --> 00:04:49.688
"Why did you do that?"

71
00:04:51.168 --> 00:04:53.289
"Because he seemed so sad."

72
00:04:54.989 --> 00:04:57.510
There was another question that Aunt Polly wanted to ask.

73
00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.451
She hesitated, almost afraid to hear the answer.

74
00:05:04.472 --> 00:05:08.793
She sat down and gathered her courage before asking, "What did he say?"

75
00:05:08.813 --> 00:05:13.534
"He said you can't always get a spouse just by asking.

76
00:05:15.035 --> 00:05:19.916
I know he wants a wife because I heard him say so, even though he spoke very quietly."

77
00:05:21.364 --> 00:05:22.205
"What did he say?"

78
00:05:22.745 --> 00:05:25.387
Aunt Polly asked again in her own soft voice.

79
00:05:25.407 --> 00:05:31.672
"He said he'd do almost anything to have one particular woman's hand and heart."

80
00:05:33.754 --> 00:05:36.636
Aunt Polly stood up hurriedly and went back to the window.

81
00:05:36.656 --> 00:05:39.258
"What's the matter, Aunt Polly?"

82
00:05:39.278 --> 00:05:42.841
"Er nothing, dear.

83
00:05:43.401 --> 00:05:46.424
It's time to move this pendant so it catches more light."
